cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "context-slim: cache-aware context pruning for LLM agent loops"
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rahmati
    given-names: Ramtin
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ramtin2000/context-slim"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/ctx-slim/"
abstract: >-
  Context pruning in LLM agent loops is universally reported in tokens removed.
  Because commercial prompt caches are prefix caches, an un-pruned conversation
  is append-only and the whole prior prompt is billed at the discounted
  cache-read rate, so any prune breaks that property and forces a re-write at a
  premium. Measured against a live API using providers' own cached-token
  counters, pruning sent 20.7% fewer tokens while costing 33-59% more
  (oldest-first +59.4%, newest-first +32.9%, n=5, bootstrap 95% CIs, all
  significant), and prune order alone accounted for 16.6% at identical token
  counts. context-slim implements the resulting break-even model as a policy
  that declines unprofitable prunes, pins the cache-activation prefix, and
  edits tool-calling turns atomically.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - prompt caching
  - context engineering
  - agents
  - inference cost
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
